@startuml f6-agent-loop-fanout
title F6 - Agent loop: events go to State Registry (historical), status updates go to Router

|AG|
start
while (more steps?) is (yes)
  :Build prompt with history, tools, env;
  :POST prompt;

  |LLM|
  :Reason;
  :Return completion OR tool_use;

  |AG|
  :Receive response;

  if (Final result?) then (yes)
    :Emit final event;
    -->[handoff] "See F8 (finalize)";
    stop
  else (no, continue)
    :Execute tool;
    :Emit tool_use event with kind=tool_use, payload=tool, args;
  endif

  |EX|
  :Capture stdout event stream;

  |EX|
  :REST POST /events to State Registry
 with task_id, kind, payload;

  |State Registry|
:Persist event in State Registry DB;

  |EX|
  :REST POST /tasks/:id/status to Router
 with status update;

  |Router|
:Update task status in Router DB;

  if (Operator control request exists in State Registry?) then (yes)
    |EX|
    :Read pending control request from State Registry;
    :Apply control (inject message, cancel, etc.);
  endif

  |AG|
  :Perform tool call (if applicable);

  :Send next prompt to LLM;

  |LLM|
  :Return next completion;

  |AG|
endwhile (no)

note right
  Historical events: EX -> State Registry (canonical record).
  Live status: EX -> Router (queue assignment update).
  Operator WS subscribes to State Registry via GW (see F3).
  No broker in this loop.
end note

stop

@enduml
